htmlparts.append('</div></section><section><h2>What makes the next session consistent</h2><div class="rule"><p class="flowline">Read current state → classify the request → select applicable gates → perform the next authorized action → save the new state.</p><p>One current record per variant identifies source/cut, transcript, brand/style, engine/entry point, scene decisions, dependencies, review evidence and export/hash. CONTEXT stays short and points to that record. A scene change reopens that scene; a shared change reopens its dependents; a cut change reopens timing work.</p><p>A small correction skips fresh intake. Render-only work reuses current preview evidence and still verifies the new output. Research and technical fixes belong to the agent. User approval is recorded from an actual decision, never inferred from a passed tool.</p></div><h2>Validation and remaining human work</h2><p>Current audit: __TEST_COUNT__ regression tests pass, including fresh and intake scaffolds in both engines. The Enzo source check predates the user-requested project reset; the new project starts from the retained original recording. The earlier isolated Uplabs Remotion pilot remains separate evidence. Cvander production exports remain byte-identical. <a href="PIPELINE-READINESS-2026-09-20.md">Readiness report and Enzo handoff</a>.</p><p>Paper Collage is an installed style contract with a Remotion production reference. A HyperFrames Paper Collage style pilot and complete portable component library are not claimed. Resource relevance, visual quality, speech accuracy, voice sync and actual platform preview still require contextual review.</p></section><footer>Evidence: ../../archivo/auditoria-pipeline/2026-09-20-readiness/ and the earlier .audit/remotion-pilot/. No production video was rebuilt, upgraded or published. Existing project issues remain visible; this audit does not silently repair past episodes. This viewer and SVGs work offline.</footer></main>')
